# Line-ending policy. Without this file `core.autocrlf` decides, and a binary
# asset that happens to contain no NUL byte (a small uncompressed PDF, for
# instance) is classified as *text* and rewritten on checkout: on Windows every
# LF became CRLF, the file grew from 1431 to 1505 bytes, and the contract service
# — which re-hashes the template on every read — refused it as
# CONTRACT_TEMPLATE_UNAVAILABLE. Byte-exact assets must never go through a
# line-ending filter.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tar   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
